*.swp
*.swo
**/__pycache__/

# Secure boot key material and build artifacts - must never be committed. The
# flow writes under scripts/secure_boot/files/, except the AUTH_JTAG message
# (one level up). All key material lives under files/keys/ - one rule covers it.
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/keys/
# _gen_keys.sh's default tree. Losing psk1_rsa.pem bricks every board burned with
# its PPK0 hash, and this sits in the working tree - back it up off this checkout.
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/secure_boot_keys/
# any other key tree kept beside it (per-board copies, rekey test trees)
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/secure_boot_keys*/
# key_manager.sh's lock file
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/.key_manager.lock
# key_manager.sh workspaces: files/workspaces/<project>/<state>/ holds the key set, the Developer's
# package, the flash tars and the work trees. Never in the repo; back keys/ up off it.
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/workspaces/
# a flash tar dropped at the repo root (bare-tree runs write it to the cwd): its
# provision_BOOT.BIN can carry a red key in the clear
/flash-*.tar
# bootgen writes the pmcdata key into its CWD (files/) regardless of the BIF
# path - the one key file that cannot be kept under keys/
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/*.nky
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/xsa_files/
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/bootgen_log.txt
# make_zip.sh staging tree: a full copy of the boot materials, rebuilt from
# scratch on every run. The zip itself lands in the project root, outside this
# repo, so it needs no rule here.
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/_pkg/
# per-run step logs from files/_sign_secure_boot.sh; they quote key material
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/logs/
# authenticatedJtagImage-rsa.bin: signed with the primary key, unlocks JTAG on a
# provisioned board. Belongs to the key owner, never in the repo.
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/*.bin
meta-mango-xilinx/scripts/secure_boot/files/*.bin

# wrap-package.sh output: the tgz handed to the Key Manager, plus the staged tree
# it was built from. Build artifacts, remade on every run.
deliverable/
